    "result_text": "The change is in, and `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **Rounding is now half to even.** The live due on screen uses it (`due()` in `features/rates/Rates.tsx`), and so does the figure the server freezes when a claim is settled (`ApplyClaimAction.java`, now `RoundingMode.HALF_EVEN`). Settled claims still show their frozen figure.\n- **A claim's figure** comes from one new helper, `claimDue` in `features/claims/Claims.tsx`: the frozen figure if the claim is settled, otherwise its live due at the rate in force on the claim's date. The claim row and the totals both use it, so they always agree.\n- **A person's due-total** (`features/people/People.tsx`) is now the sum of the rounded figures of their open and settled claims, and 0.00 if they have none. It shows n/a when their grade has no rate today, unless one of those claims is settled with a frozen figure; then it's the sum of the figures there are.\n- **The sheet's due-total** is still everyone's due-total added up, and n/a entries are skipped.\n\n**One choice to check:** if a person's grade has a rate today but one of their open claims has no rate on its own date, that claim's n/a figure is left out of the sum. The request doesn't cover this case and the tests don't exercise it.\n\nNo database or audit changes were needed.",
